[2026-08-12] Training-reproduction audit findings

- Resume is continuous: continuation logging starts at epoch 15 and the final
  checkpoint records epoch 29; optimizer state has 404 entries and scheduler
  state is present.
- Local parameters changed materially across epochs 5→15 and 15→30. This rules
  out a frozen model or skipped optimizer-step explanation.
- The local run used effective batch size 1 with no gradient accumulation. The
  supplied trained checkpoint records world size 4 and per-process batch size 2
  (effective batch size 8). The external loop hard-codes one optimizer update
  per microbatch and does not scale learning rate, so the local run made eight
  times as many noisier AdamW updates per dataset epoch at the same LR.
- Local epoch 30 was still before the first schedule milestone (31); the
  supplied high-AP checkpoint is from epoch 75 and records milestones 31 and
  66. The two runs are not controlled training comparisons.
- ED-Pose loading has the same 723 learned-tensor overlap expected by the
  supplied trained model. The eight unused `pose_vis_embed` tensors and 18 new
  DiffusionRegPose heads are expected architecture differences, not evidence of
  a failed initialization.
- EMA updates are commented out. This is an upstream defect, but evaluator
  calls use the raw model, so stale EMA weights do not explain the observed AP.
- Next controlled experiment: fresh effective-batch-8 training via tested
  gradient accumulation (or physical batch 8), without changing matcher,
  coordinates, decoder, or loss behavior.

